-number><kind>A1</kind></document-id><sources><source category="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>ASHTON WALLACE T. ET AL.: 'Irreversible enzyme inhibitors. 198. Diaminodihydro-s-triazines and diaminopyrimidines bearing substituted (ureidomethyl)phenyl substituents as reversible inhibitors of dihydrofolate reductase' J. MED. CHEM., vol. 16, no. 5, 1973, pages 453 - 456, XP002927662</text><sources><source category="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1142868A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><last-name>MITSUBISHI CHEM CORP</last-name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>MITSUBISHI CHEMICAL CORPORATION</last-name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><last-name>ANDO RYOICHI</last-name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><last-name>CHIBA NORIKO</last-name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>ANDO, RYOICHI</last-name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>CHIBA, NORIKO</last-name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Amide derivatives represented by general formula (I), which have an activity against Helicobacter pylori and are useful as the active ingredient of drugs, pharmaceutically acceptable salts thereof or solvates or hydrates of the same, wherein R&lt;1&gt; represents (1) C1-10 alkyl optionally substituted by optionally substituted C6-14 aryl, fluorenyl or a heterocyclic group, (2) optionally substituted C6-14 aryl, or (3) an optionally substituted heterocyclic group; R&lt;2&gt;, R&lt;3&gt; and R&lt;4&gt; independently represent each hydrogen or C1-5 alkyl; X represents oxygen or N-R&lt;5&gt; (wherein R&lt;5&gt; represents hydrogen or C1-5 alkyl); and Y represents oxygen or sulfur, provided that the compound where R&lt;1&gt; is benzyl, R&lt;2&gt; and R&lt;3&gt; are each hydrogen, R&lt;4&gt; is propyl and X and Y are each oxygen is excluded.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Cette invention se rapporte à des dérivés d'amide, qui sont représentés par la formule générale (I), qui ont une action contre l'Helicobacter pylori et qui sont utiles comme principe actif de médicaments, ainsi qu'à des sels pharmaceutiquement acceptables de ces dérivés ou des solvates ou hydrates de ceux-ci. Dans cette formule, R&lt;1&gt; représente: (1) alkyle C1-10 éventuellement substitué par aryle C6-14 éventuellement substitué, fluorényle ou un groupe hétérocyclique; (2) aryle C6-14 éventuellement substitué; ou (3) un groupe hétérocyclique éventuellement substitué; R&lt;2&gt;, R&lt;3&gt; et R&lt;4&gt; représentent séparément chacun hydrogène ou alkyle C1-5; X représente oxygène ou N-R&lt;5&gt; (R&lt;5&gt; représentant hydrogène ou alkyle C1-5); et Y représente oxygène ou soufre, à condition d'exclure le composé dans lequel R&lt;1&gt; représente benzyle, R&lt;2&gt; et R&lt;3&gt; représentent chacun hydrogène, R&lt;4&gt; représente propyle et X et Y représente chacun oxygène.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.